      "side": 1,
      "message": "For a tall Jacobian, max(num_rows, num_cols) - null_space_rank keeps up to num_rows - num_cols more modes than requested. In TruncatedRank (8x6 J, null_space_rank \u003d 1) it gives 7, so all six modes are kept and the expected covariance, which drops the smallest eigenvector, no longer matches. J\u0027J is num_cols x num_cols whatever the number of rows, so its null space counts against num_cols, and for square and wide Jacobians max(num_rows, num_cols) is num_cols anyway.",
